WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.530
Lötschental, in the
Swiss canton of Valais.

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.650
Above the village of Blatten
sits the Birch Glacier.

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.310
Rockfalls from the Kleines
Nesthorn piled debris onto it.

4
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.370
Authorities estimate
over 10 million tonnes.

5
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:19.410
From 2019, the glacier's lower
front advanced about 50 metres.

6
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.770
On 28 May 2025, the glacier collapsed.

7
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.370
Ice and rock buried a
considerable part of the village.

8
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.130
In 2002, a glacier
collapse at Kolka-Karmadon,

9
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.750
in Russia, killed 125 people.

10
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.450
At Blatten, one man died.

11
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.950
Why did only one person die?

12
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.710
In this mission, you'll
read the valley's geology,

13
00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.970
its slopes and its landforms.

14
00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.990
Then you'll trace how the glacier changed,

15
00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.270
over years, minutes and seconds.

16
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.360
Your mission: explain why only
one person died at Blatten.
